FFLs as statistically significant subgraphs in TRNs: FFL motifs have been shown to be the “building blocks”, i.e., they are over-represented subgraphs in biological networks like TRNs20,27,28. We used a motif detection tool, called FANMOD11 to show that some of the abundant 4–, 5– and 6–node motifs contain FFL motifs (see Appendix B of Supplementary Materials). We intuit that the information flow in TRNs can be effectively analyzed w.r.t. the FFL motifs.

