The validated and nearly complete TRNs of Escherichia coli (E. coli) and Saccharomyces cerevisiae (S.cerevisiae) were extracted from GeneNetWeaver34. This tool generates topologies by extracting modules based on biological interactions in E. coli and S.cerevisiae. Homo sapiens (human) and Mus musculus (mouse) TRNs were obtained from the TRRUST database35; these two TRNs catalogue the partially known validated interactions between TFs and genes in these organisms. The orders, sizes and graph densities (showing the sparse nature) of the four TRN topologies considered are summarized in Table 1.Table 1
